"{\"url\":\"https://registry.isometric.com/project/prj_1JZ0ZD3JN1S0SHW9\",\"title\":\"Project Cajueiro — Isometric\",\"head\":[\"VALIDATED\",\"EW\",\"1,000Y+\",\"Project Cajueiro\",\"Mombak\",\"ISSUED\",\"46.94\",\"BUFFER POOL\",\"0.939\",\"CREDITING PERIOD\",\"19 Jul 2024 to 31 Aug 2027\",\"Summary\"],\"issued_header\":\"46.94\",\"buffer_header\":\"0.939\",\"crediting\":\"19 Jul 2024 to 31 Aug 2027\",\"verifier\":\"350Solutions\",\"code\":\"68X8\",\"approval\":\"01 Apr 2026\",\"protocol_current\":\"Enhanced Weathering in Agriculture v1.2\",\"protocol_baseline\":\"Enhanced Weathering in Agriculture v1.1\",\"cert_issued\":\"46.94\",\"cert_retired\":\"46\",\"cert_buffer\":\"0.939\",\"reversal\":\"The risk of reversal for this project has been assessed as very low. This means that 2% of certificates issued for this project are allocated to Mombak's buffer pool.\\n\\nTo date, this project has contributed 0.939 certificates to the buffer pool which holds a total of 0.939 certificates.\\n\\nMombak has no reversals to date.\",\"showing\":[\"Showing 1 of 1\",\"Showing 4 of 4\",\"Showing 1 of 1\"],\"tables\":[{\"heads\":[\"Name\",\"Category\",\"Validated\"],\"rows\":[[\"Basalto São Francisco (Copy)\",\"Mineral & rock\",\"01 Apr 2026\"]]},{\"heads\":[\"Submission date\",\"Title\",\"Download\"],\"rows\":[[\"01 Apr 2026\",\"Validation and Verification Report\",\"PDF | ->\"],[\"01 Apr 2026\",\"GHG Statement\",\"PDF | ->\"],[\"01 Apr 2026\",\"PDD\",\"PDF | ->\"],[\"19 Mar 2026\",\"Public Comment Period Summary\",\"PDF | ->\"]]},{\"heads\":[\"Issue date\",\"Issued\",\"Buffer pool\",\"Supplier allocation\"],\"rows\":[[\"01 Apr 2026\",\"46.94\",\"0.939\",\"46.001\"]]}],\"links\":[{\"h\":\"/supplier/spl_1JWY4JWJK1S05RE6\",\"t\":\"Mombak\"},{\"h\":\"https://350solutions.com\",\"t\":\"350Solutions\"},{\"h\":\"/protocol/enhanced-weathering-agriculture/1.2\",\"t\":\"Enhanced Weathering in Agriculture v1.2\"},{\"h\":\"/protocol/enhanced-weathering-agriculture/1.1\",\"t\":\"Enhanced Weathering in Agriculture v1.1\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JWY4JWJK1S05RE6/prj_1JZ0ZD3JN1S0SHW9/pjd_1KN436J6T1S0030J/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"Project Design Document | 01 Apr 2026\"},{\"h\":\"/ghg-entry/rmv_1KFEF0DBC1S0AM08?tab=calculation-view\",\"t\":\"See GHG entry →\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JWY4JWJK1S05RE6/prj_1JZ0ZD3JN1S0SHW9/pjd_1KN4FWTW21S0T9M5/validation_and_verification_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JWY4JWJK1S05RE6/prj_1JZ0ZD3JN1S0SHW9/pjd_1KN439RBM1S0KQW7/ghg_statement.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JWY4JWJK1S05RE6/prj_1JZ0ZD3JN1S0SHW9/pjd_1KN436J6T1S0030J/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JWY4JWJK1S05RE6/prj_1JZ0ZD3JN1S0SHW9/pjd_1KM5Q8HTD1S0S2E9/public_comment_period_summary.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"}],\"text\":\"VALIDATED\\nEW\\n1,000Y+\\nProject Cajueiro\\nMombak\\nISSUED\\n46.94\\nBUFFER POOL\\n0.939\\nCREDITING PERIOD\\n19 Jul 2024 to 31 Aug 2027\\nSummary\\nRemoval method\\nCalculation overview\\nFeedstocks\\nProject documentation\\nCertificates\\nReversal risk\\nSummary\\n\\nThis project applies Enhanced Rock Weathering (ERW) to commercial agricultural fields at Fazenda Cajueiro in Brazil. Finely ground basalt, certified as a soil remineralizer by Brazil’s Ministry of Agriculture, is applied to commercial agricultural fields using standard farm equipment. As the basalt weathers in soil, it releases calcium and magnesium that react with atmospheric CO₂ to form dissolved bicarbonate, which is transported through drainage pathways for long-term carbon storage. Carbon removal is quantified using direct, soil-based measurements supported by field controls and accredited laboratory analysis.\\n\\nPROJECT DETAILS\\nCurrent verifier\\n350Solutions\\n->\\nProject code\\n68X8\\nApproval date\\n01 Apr 2026\\nCurrent protocol version\\nEnhanced Weathering in Agriculture v1.2\\nBaseline protocol version\\nEnhanced Weathering in Agriculture v1.1\\nSUSTAINABLE DEVELOPMENT GOALS\\n⌘ + scroll to zoom\\nProject Cajueiro\\nHow carbon is being removed\\n\\nEnhanced Weathering (EW) accelerates the Earth's natural chemical weathering process to remove carbon dioxide from the atmosphere. In chemical weathering, carbon dioxide dissolved in rainwater reacts with minerals in rocks, partly dissolving them and producing stable bicarbonate ions. These bicarbonate ions are transported by rivers to the ocean, where they are safely stored for thousands of years. EW is typically carried out by spreading crushed reactive rocks or minerals on croplands.\\n\\nProject Design Document\\n01 Apr 2026\\nCalculation overview\\nCalculations demonstrating 46.94 tCO₂e removed from Project Cajueiro on 24 Feb 2025\\nSee GHG entry →\\nNet CO₂e Removed\\n46.938 tCO₂e\\nSequestrations\\n65.167 tCO₂e\\n-\\nActivities\\n18.229 tCO₂e\\n⌘ + scroll to zoom\\nView full screen\\nFeedstocks\\n\\nFeedstocks are the validated input materials that have been used for this project.\\n\\nName\\tCategory\\tValidated\\nBasalto São Francisco (Copy)\\tMineral & rock\\t01 Apr 2026\\nShowing 1 of 1\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nProject documentation\\nSubmission date\\tTitle\\tDownload\\n01 Apr 2026\\tValidation and Verification Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n01 Apr 2026\\tGHG Statement\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n01 Apr 2026\\tPDD\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n19 Mar 2026\\tPublic Comment Period Summary\\tPDF\\n->\\nShowing 4 of 4\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nCertificates\\nIssued\\n46.94\\nRetired\\n46\\nBuffer pool\\n0.939\\nCrediting period\\n19 Jul 2024 to 31 Aug 2027\\nIssuances\\nRetirements\\nIssue date\\tIssued\\tBuffer pool\\tSupplier allocation\\n01 Apr 2026\\t46.94\\t0.939\\t46.001\\nShowing 1 of 1\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nReversal risk\\n\\nThe risk of reversal for this project has been assessed as very low. This means that 2% of certificates issued for this project are allocated to Mombak's buffer pool.\\n\\nTo date, this project has contributed 0.939 certificates to the buffer pool which holds a total of 0.939 certificates.\\n\\nMombak has no reversals to date.\\n\\nLearn more about reversal risk\"}"